\begin{align*}
(x - h)^2 + (y - k)^2 &= r^2.
\end{align*}
The points of tangency solve $x^2 = x^2 + (y - k)^2$, which simplifies to $(y - k)^2 = 0$ or $y = k$. Since the circle is tangent to the parabola, the equation of the tangent line is
\begin{align*}
y &= x^2
\text{ where } x = h.
\end{align*}
So the point of tangency is
\begin{align*}
(h, h^2).
\end{align*}
